   $q$According to the passage, why does the rider at the front work the hardest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That rider pushes most of the air out of the way for the group.","is_correct":true},{"text":"That rider must watch the road and steer for everyone behind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"That rider is always the strongest member of the whole team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"That rider pedals at a faster speed than the riders behind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$That rider pushes most of the air out of the way for the group.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 says a cyclist must push air out of the way and "the rider at the front does most of that work." Teammates take turns at the front, so it is not always the strongest rider.$q$, 'draft', 'b282c102-d8f5-538b-9475-b9d1ae229035')
